  <question type="stack">
    <name>
      <text>Indefinite integral of polynomials</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Find the antiderivative of the function \( \displaystyle f(x)= {@f_t@}\)</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle F(x) = \) [[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="html">
      <text><![CDATA[<h3>Worked solution</h3>
<p>Suppose we have a function of the form \( \displaystyle f(x)=x^{n}\), its antiderivative can be computed as,</p>
<p> \(  \displaystyle  \int x^n\, dx=\frac{x^{n+1}}{n+1}+c\), where \(\ c\) is the constant of integration</p>
<p>Therefore, the antiderivative of \(  \displaystyle {@f_t@}\) will be,</p>
<p>\(  \displaystyle  \int {@f_t@}\, dt = {@ta@} \)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
